---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { site, isTodo } from '../config/site';
import { emailUrl, phoneUrl, whatsappUrl, withBase } from '../utils/links';

const email = emailUrl('Refund request');
const phone = phoneUrl();
const whatsapp = whatsappUrl('refund');
const calendly = !isTodo(site.contact.calendly) ? site.contact.calendly : null;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Refunds Policy"
  description="How refunds work for InnovaTech World courses and services: when you can get a refund, when you cannot, and how to request one."
>
  <article class="prose refunds">
    <h1>Refunds Policy</h1>
    <p class="muted">Last updated: 13 November 2026</p>

    <p>
      This policy explains when you can and cannot get a refund from InnovaTech World, {site.location},
      for our <strong>courses</strong> (the Knowledge Hub) and our <strong>services</strong> (done-for-you
      work and talent placement). We want you to be happy with what you pay for, and we also need clear,
      fair rules so we can plan and deliver good work. This policy sits alongside our
      <a href={withBase('/terms/')}>Terms of Use</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Courses (Knowledge Hub)</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Because course materials are unlocked and available to you <strong>immediately on payment</strong>,
        course fees are generally <strong>non-refundable</strong>.
      </li>
      <li>
        If you were <strong>charged in error</strong> (for example, charged twice), or you
        <strong>cannot access</strong> a course you paid for and we cannot fix it, contact us within
        <strong>7 days</strong> of payment and we will resolve it or refund you.
      </li>
      <li>
        A discount code or free pass has no cash value and cannot be refunded or exchanged for money.
      </li>
      <li>
        Payments are processed by <strong>Paystack</strong>. Approved refunds are returned to your original
        payment method; the time to appear in your account depends on your bank or card provider.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Services (done-for-you work)</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Our service rates are quoted <strong>per hour in US Dollars (USD)</strong>. You <strong>pay in
        Nigerian Naira</strong>, at the current Naira equivalent of the Dollar amount at the time of payment.
      </li>
      <li>
        To begin, we usually agree an estimated number of hours and take a <strong>deposit</strong> or
        <strong>prepaid hours</strong>. Because this reserves our time, it is
        <strong>non-refundable once work has started</strong>.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Unused prepaid hours</strong> (hours you paid for but we have not yet worked) can be refunded
        or carried over to future work, your choice.
      </li>
      <li>
        If we have <strong>not yet started</strong>, you may cancel and request a refund, minus any work
        already done or costs already incurred on your behalf.
      </li>
      <li>
        If we <strong>cannot deliver</strong> what we agreed in writing, you are entitled to a refund for the
        part we did not deliver. Hours already worked and delivered are non-refundable.
      </li>
      <li>
        Change-of-mind, a change in your own plans, or delays caused by missing information or approvals from
        your side are not grounds for a refund of work already done.
      </li>
      <li>
        Because you pay the Naira equivalent of the Dollar amount, exchange-rate movements between payment and
        any refund are not refundable; approved refunds are returned in Naira at the rate used when you paid.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Talent placement</h2>
    <p>
      Fees for recruiting and placing talent are agreed in writing for each engagement, including any trial
      period and what happens if a placement does not work out. Those written terms govern refunds for that
      engagement.
    </p>

    <h2>How to request a refund</h2>
    <p>
      Send us a message with your name, what you paid for, the amount, and the Paystack reference or
      transaction date. We aim to respond within <strong>5 working days</strong> and to complete approved
      refunds within <strong>14 working days</strong>.
    </p>
    <p>
      {email && (<a href={email}>{site.contact.email}</a>)}
      {email && (phone || whatsapp) && ' · '}
      {phone && (<a href={phone}>{site.contact.phone}</a>)}
      {phone && whatsapp && ' · '}
      {whatsapp && (<a href={whatsapp} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">WhatsApp</a>)}
      {calendly && (<> · <a href={calendly} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">book a call</a></>)}
    </p>

    <h2>Your statutory rights</h2>
    <p>
      Nothing in this policy removes any rights you have under applicable Nigerian consumer law. If this
      policy and the law differ, the law applies.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this policy from time to time. We will post the new version here and change the
      "last updated" date above. The policy that applied when you paid is the one that governs your purchase.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .refunds { margin-inline: auto; }
  .refunds .muted { color: var(--color-muted); }
</style>
